Dear Glenn,

At 10:50 AM 6/4/2002 +0100, Glenn.Treacy at ilim.com wrote:

> Does anyone know how I can place inverted commas in a string in S-Plus 2000
> NT4. I want to produce a string like "function("UK","USA","Europe")"?

If I understand properly what you want, you can enclose the string in 
single, rather than double, quotes:

        'function("UK","USA","Europe")'

or reverse the single and double quotes:

        "function('UK','USA','Europe')"

or escape the quote characters (with backslashes):

        "function(\"UK\",\"USA\",\"Europe\")"

John

