A GEE-type approach with coefficients estimated from a working independence 
model can work quite well for your situation.  One such approach is to use the 
Design library's lrm function, then pass the fit object to the robcov or 
bootcov function which both implement intra-cluster correlation adjustments for 
the variance-covariance matrix.  I think that the cluster bootstrap works a 
little better than the cluster sandwich estimator (robcov).  See the help file 
in robcov or bootcov for an example like yours.  -Frank Harrell

