Hardly 100 independent observations, though!

>   We also set na.action to na.omit and contrasts to 'treatment'; two other
> options whose default values were a mistake.

R has those two, and people are continually making mistakes with model
selection because of na.omit.  I would not advocate using na.omit, even
with the much more extensive internal checking that R has for consistency
when comparing models.  In any case, missing values need thought, not
automation.

