This is surely a wonderful list. Thanks to all who replied. The following
solution provided by Bill Pikounis works great:

You could use factor to reset the "ordering" of the levels, for example:

> set.seed(13)
> response <- rnorm(15,100,20)
> oldfactor <- factor(rep(c("C","L","H"), times=5))
> newfactor <- factor(oldfactor, levels=c("L","C","H"))
>  
> levels(oldfactor)
[1] "C" "H" "L"
> levels(newfactor)
[1] "L" "C" "H"

 
