From hastie at stat.stanford.edu  Wed Jun  5 23:41:28 2002
From: hastie at stat.stanford.edu (Trevor Hastie)
Date: Wed, 05 Jun 2002 16:41:28 -0700
Subject: gam.control and glm.control
Message-ID: <004001c20cea$84890cd0$d3bb42ab@yacht>

It came to my attention recently that the control 
parameters used in gam,

such as the convergence threshold and maximum 
iteration count, are

rather out of date. These were set in 1990 when 
computers were much slower than today.

The function that delivers these values 
gam.control(). The easiest way to change the defaults

is to change this function. Below is a modified 
version of gam.control that sets the defaults as follows:

 

 gam.control()
$epsilon:
[1] 
1e-07

 

$maxit:
[1] 30

 

$bf.epsilon:
[1] 1e-07

 

$bf.maxit:
[1] 30

 

$trace:
[1] F

 

Likewise a modified version of glm.control now sets 
its defaults to 

 

 glm.control()
$epsilon:
[1] 
1e-07

 

$maxit:
[1] 30

 

$trace:
[1] F

"glm.control"

