1) There is no anova method for glmmPQL, and I have no idea where you got
the idea that anova could be used with glmmPQL.

2) By definition, glmmPQL does not compute a log-likelihood nor AIC, so
you can't do likelihood ratio tests.

More or less the same comments apply to nlme, which gives an approximation
to the log-likelihood and AIC, and that approximation can be poor.

