Yes, there is a "science" to this. It is called Independent Component 
Analysis (ICA). It exploits higher order moments such as kurtosis to 
"factor" distributions out of mixtures. It is applied to such problems as 
"blind-source separation" (e.g. separating voices in a conversation etc).

Here is a good overview of ICA: 
http://www.cis.hut.fi/projects/compneuro/whatisica.html

I believe there is a FastICA routine in CRAN. Do an "ICA" search on the 
R-site for a few more R implementations. (Some of it ported from MATLAB).

Hth,
John Day
PhD Candidate
Florida Tech

